Organizer --> U4 : read only
Administrator --> A1
Administrator --> A2
Administrator --> A3
Administrator --> A4
Administrator --> A5
Administrator --> A6
Administrator --> A7
Administrator --> A8
Administrator --> A9
Administrator --> U1 : read only
Administrator --> U3 : read only
Administrator --> U4 : read only
System --> S1
System --> S2
System --> S3
System --> S4
System --> S5
System --> S6
System --> S7
U5 ..> Pricing : <<include>>
U5 ..> Access : <<include>>
SubscriptionChoice ..> U5 : <<extend>>
Redeem ..> U5 : <<extend>>
Confirm ..> U5 : <<extend>>\nAUTO and zero/subscription
Confirm ..> U6 : <<extend>>\nsuccessful payment
Confirm ..> O8 : <<extend>>\napproved, no card payment due
Confirm ..> S5 : <<include>>
Confirm ..> Notify : <<include>>
U7 ..> Restore : <<include>>
O9 ..> Restore : <<include>>
S1 ..> Restore : <<include>>
S7 ..> Restore : <<extend>>\nprevious successful payment
O6 ..> Restore : <<include>>
O6 ..> Notify : <<include>>
A5 ..> Restore : <<include>>
Restore ..> Notify : <<include>>
note bottom of ActiveHub
Green: implemented mandatory behavior; verification scope is in FINAL_ACCEPTANCE.md.
Grey [S] cases are optional and are not part of this delivery.
Every protected action checks server role, owner and active account.
System S1-S7 are mandatory IDs. Q-01 through Q-04 use the recorded owner decisions.
Q-05 classification follows the latest decision in ASSUMPTIONS.md.
end note
@enduml
